    location: "Conference alcove",
    narration: "Aldrin sits with Marites over a coffee and explains something she needs to understand before her first independent shift. Surveyors do not grade intentions. They do not care that you meant to do the right thing. They review evidence chains: risk was recognized, action was taken, escalation was completed, and documentation shows exactly what happened and when. If any link in that chain is missing, the rest does not matter. A well-intentioned clinician with incomplete documentation is indistinguishable from a careless one in a survey record. That is why documentation is not bureaucracy. It is the proof that you did what you said you did.",
