    location: "Patient home — kitchen near-miss response",
    narration: "Help Marites respond correctly. She has just discovered that Mr. Henderson has been double-dosing because two prior visit notes contained conflicting medication instructions. He has not yet taken today's dose. Marites has four options. What is the most defensible immediate response? Option A: Correct the patient's understanding immediately at the bedside, update the medication schedule, call the supervising clinician during this same visit, and document the near-miss, the corrected education, the teach-back result, and the revised care plan. Option B: Correct the patient's understanding now, document the correction and the updated schedule at the end of the day after all visits are complete. Option C: Ask the patient's family to monitor his medication taking closely and call the agency if any confusion continues. Option D: Wait to adjust the medication instructions until the next scheduled physician order update, to avoid providing instructions that contradict a prior documented order.",
